\section{Service Process}
\label{sec-1}
\subsection{Collect information from client}
\label{sec-1-1}
This step is collecting contemporary operations information
from the client, and would be a combination of questionnaires
and interviews.
\subsection{Analyze client information}
\label{sec-1-2}
This step is giving some thought to what would work best for
this client.
\subsection{Develop operations package}
\label{sec-1-3}
This step is picking what operations framework and lexicon
would work best for the client, and preparing their
documentation.
\subsubsection{Determine operations framework}
\label{sec-1-3-1}
This step is picking what hierarchy, system of reporting, task
distribution, and so on, the organization should use.
\subsubsection{Determine operations lexicon}
\label{sec-1-3-2}
This step is picking what language the client's documentation
should be provided in.  (Software development, business ops,
emotional, funny).
\subsubsection{Template operations package}
\label{sec-1-3-3}
This step is applying the previous decisions to a template to
produce the client's documentation.
\subsubsection{Specify company procedures}
\label{sec-1-3-4}
This step is providing specific procedures for the client's
operations, in the style of its templated documentation.
\subsection{Prepare operations package}
\label{sec-1-4}
This step is preparing the final documentation in appropriate
formats.
\subsection{Submit operations package.}
\label{sec-1-5}
This step is providing the package to Lynn for review.
